I replaced the type-specific wrapper call with a direct `SetFieldValue` call, passing the parameter by address. This eliminates one function call and a temporary array copy while preserving the exact field/subfield semantics.

```cpp
    void SetEndTimezoneOffset(FIT_SINT16 endTimezoneOffset)
    {
        SetFieldValue(3, 0, &endTimezoneOffset, 1);
    }
```